*Razavi Fundamentals Microelectronics CMOS Models
*Technology CMOS 180nm
* Libreria unica (modelo DC/AC + parametros de ruido). Los .MODEL son identicos a los de
* ngspice/Razavi/razavi_cmos.lib excepto kf/af (ver abajo); cambia ademas la forma de declarar w, l, m en los subckt.
* Parametros de ruido (didacticos, calibrados contra sky130 y gf180mcuD, ver ngspice/Razavi/Extraccion_KF_AF.ipynb):
*   kf, af : ruido flicker del Level 1.
*   OJO: LTspice y ngspice NO usan la misma formula para kf. Medido en LTspice (Noise_A/B/C.raw):
*        S_vin,fl = kf / (f * W * L * Cox)     [V^2/Hz]  (referido a la entrada, no depende de Id)
*     ngspice:  S_id,fl = kf * Id^af / (f * W * L * Cox^2)  ->  S_vin,fl = kf / (2*kp*W^2*Cox^2*(1+lambda*VDS) * f)
*   Por eso el kf de esta libreria es distinto al de ngspice/Razavi/razavi_cmos.lib. Con W=1u, L=0.18u
*   da el mismo ruido flicker en ambos simuladores (NMOS 43 uV/rtHz a 1 Hz, fc ~51 MHz;
*   PMOS 21 uV/rtHz a 1 Hz, fc ~5.9 MHz). Para otra geometria hay que recalcular kf.
*   Los kf/af NO afectan a las simulaciones DC/AC/transitorias, solo a .noise.
* Variante nch_rs / xnchr (y pch_rs / xpchr): igual que nch (pch) con rd = rs = 200 ohm (ruido termico 4kT/R de cada una).

.MODEL nch NMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=100u vto=0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=2.87e-24 af=1

.MODEL pch PMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=50u vto=-0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=6.7e-25 af=1

.MODEL nch_rs NMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=100u vto=0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=2.87e-24 af=1
+rd=200 rs=200

.MODEL pch_rs PMOS LEVEL = 1
+kp=50u vto=-0.4
+gamma=0.4 lambda=0.1
+phi=0.3 tox=40e-10
+cgso = 9.548e-10 cgdo = 9.548e-10
+cj=9.81e-4 cjsw=1.19e-10
+mjsw=0 mj=0
+kf=6.7e-25 af=1
+rd=200 rs=200

.subckt xnch D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B nch l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends

.subckt xpch D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B pch l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends

.subckt xnchr D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B nch_rs l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends

.subckt xpchr D G S B

.param l=0.18u w=2u m=1
.param wd = 0.48e-6
.param ad = 'w*wd'
.param as = 'w*wd'
.param ps = '2*w+2*wd'
.param pd = '2*w+2*wd'

M1 D G S B pch_rs l=l w=w ad=ad as=as pd=pd ps=ps m=m
.ends
